#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pr-watch: block until a GitHub PR needs the agent, then say why and exit.

    pr-watch <pr> [--repo owner/name] [--interval 300] [--once]
    pr-watch --check

<pr> is a PR number or URL; the repo comes from the URL, --repo, or the
current checkout. Run one background job per PR. It polls quietly and exits on
the first poll that needs a decision, so the job's exit is the wake-up. Restart
it after acting: it remembers what it already reported.

Every agent's watchers spend one account's rate limits, which Ainesh's cockpit
needs too, so a watcher is paced so that it cannot spend them. A poll reads the
PR's head by `git ls-remote`, which spends no API budget, and everything else
by REST as conditional requests: an unchanged resource answers 304, which no
limit counts. The PR itself (`pulls/<n>`, and the open-PR list a stack is
followed down by) never answers 304, since it embeds the repository's
pushed_at, so it is read only on the first poll, when the head moved or its
branch is gone, when feedback changed, when the checks changed and none is
still running, and every FULL_EVERY polls. GraphQL is read only for review
threads' resolution, which REST lacks, when the PR's review comments changed
or the PR itself is read. Every response's rate-limit headers pace the next sleep: the calls a
poll counts (averaged over the last FULL_EVERY polls), times WATCHERS watchers,
times the polls left before the bucket resets, stays under half of what that
bucket has left; when one poll of every watcher would already cross that line,
the watcher sleeps to the reset. --interval (default and minimum 300) is the
fastest cadence. A watcher re-executes itself when its file changes on disk.

A droid daemon restart kills every background job without an exit notice, so
a watcher can vanish silently. --check lists this machine's watchers: alive,
or dead without a verdict with the command that restarts it (exit 1 if any).

--once evaluates the PR a single time and reports everything open now, without
waiting: ACTION when any line needs the agent, WAIT when only waiting lines
remain, READY otherwise. Each failed optional check, and the risk assessment of
the head, is listed whatever the verdict and never sets it, since what either
means is the agent's call. It neither reads nor saves reported keys, though a
MERGED or CLOSED verdict still deletes the PR's state. Run it whenever you
need the PR's current state and immediately before merging; pin the merge to
the head sha that the verdict line ends with.

Stdout carries event lines, then one verdict line; progress goes to stderr.

  READY   exit 0  approved; every check finished and every gating check passed;
                  no unresolved review thread; no pending review; and GitHub
                  reports it mergeable (CLEAN, HAS_HOOKS, or UNSTABLE), however
                  far the base moved
  MERGED  exit 0
  ACTION  exit 1  the event lines say what needs doing
  CLOSED  exit 1
  ERROR   exit 2  bad input, another watcher holds the PR, or GitHub failed
  WAIT    exit 3  --once only: nothing gates on the agent; the waiting lines
                  name what resolves without it

Events
  check-failed  a check failed on the head; the PR author's own decision
                whether an optional failure is real. While a PR has neither
                an approval nor the e2e:run label, the E2E workflow waits by
                design, and its "E2E waits for approval" annotation says so:
                on each failed status run (the older form), or as the plan
                job's notice while the status jobs skip and their required
                checks never report. Either is a wait, not a failure
  comment, review
                a top-level comment or review posted or edited after the
                agent's latest response; comments from CI and
                deploy bots and factory-service-* accounts are skipped, since
                checks carry that news, as is Linear's linkback comment to the
                issue
  risk-assessment
                the repository's risk assessment scored the PR's head: its
                verdict and first points, once per head and verdict, however
                often its comment is rewritten. Its waiting and running
                notices, and a score of an older head, are status
  thread        a review thread that is unresolved and whose last submitted
                comment is not the agent's, outdated or not: a review drafted
                on an older commit is outdated the moment it is submitted
  pending-review
                the viewer's review is unsubmitted. GraphQL review mutations
                file the account's comments and thread replies into it, where
                only the account can read them, so its threads read as
                answered to the agent and as silent to everyone else
  conflict      the branch conflicts with its base
  behind        branch protection requires the branch to be current; GitHub
                reports BEHIND only then, so a behind PR on any other base
                stays mergeable
  unresolved    otherwise ready, but review threads are unresolved, answered
                and outdated ones included: they still block merging
  (BLOCKED)     otherwise ready, but GitHub still reports BLOCKED: a wait, since
                REST has no review decision and an approval branch protection
                does not count yet (a code owner's is missing) looks the same
  incomplete    the PR has more than 100 review threads, so READY is
                impossible to prove; check them by hand

Gating checks are the required checks of the branch the PR finally lands in:
its base, or for a stacked PR the base of the bottom PR of its stack (each
open PR from the base below it into another branch of the same repository,
followed down; a fork's PR that pulls the branch into its own copy is no part
of it). A stacked PR gates only on the ones reporting on its head, since
workflows into the landing branch often filter on it and run only once GitHub
retargets the PR there. A landing branch that requires none makes every check
gate.

Feedback events describe what is open on GitHub now, not what changed since a
run. The agent's words are exactly the comments, reviews, and thread replies
carrying AGENT_MARK; authors and commits never count, since the agent shares
an account with its user, and neither does a pending review or its comments,
which nobody else can read. Its latest response is the newest of those
anywhere on the PR. A thread stays settled while a marked reply has its last
word; a top-level comment or review is settled by any later response, until
its author edits it. A bot's edit reopens too: a QA bot rewrites its report
in place when a run fails (factory-mono#28661 went from passing to FAILED
32/34 in an edit). Status bots, whose in-place rewrites only repeat what checks
say, are skipped whatever they post.

State lives in $XDG_STATE_HOME/pr-watch (default ~/.local/state/pr-watch): the
keys the watcher has reported, so a restart never re-wakes on what it already
reported. There is no first-run baseline: a first run reports everything open.
Its required/ directory caches each base's required checks for every process,
revalidated by ETag on each process's first read.
Feedback is keyed by comment and its version, its latest edit or else its
posting (a thread by its last comment), so a new reply or an edit wakes the
watcher once; a pending review by its comment count, so each reply
filed into it wakes again; gate events are keyed by head and base. A MERGED or
CLOSED exit deletes the PR's state.

Adapted from pr-wait in https://github.com/t3dotgg/tstack:

  MIT License

  Copyright (c) 2026 Theo Browne

  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
  of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
  copies or substantial portions of the Software.

  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
  SOFTWARE.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import hashlib
import html
import json
import math
import os
import random
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from collections.abc import Callable
from datetime import UTC, datetime
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, NoReturn
from urllib.parse import quote

Json = dict[str, Any]
SELF = Path(__file__).resolve()

STATE_DIR = (
    Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".local" / "state")
    / "pr-watch"
)
# The agent ends every reply it posts with this. It often shares one GitHub
# account with the user, so the author alone cannot tell their comments apart.
AGENT_MARK = "<!-- agent-reply -->"
NEVER = datetime.min.replace(tzinfo=UTC)
# Service accounts are GitHub Users that automation drives, such as the snyk
# scanner, so their author type alone reads as human.
SERVICE_PREFIX = "factory-service-"
STATUS_BOTS = (
    SERVICE_PREFIX,
    "github-actions",
    "vercel",
    "netlify",
    "railway",
    "cloudflare",
    "codecov",
)
# Linear's bot links every PR to its issue in one comment opening with this
# marker: a link, not feedback. Its other comments still count.
LINEAR_BOT = "linear-code"
LINKBACK = "<!-- linear-linkback -->"
# The repository's risk assessment is one github-actions comment opening with
# this marker, rewritten in place on every push: "Waiting" and "Running" until
# it scores the head, then its verdict and the head it scored.
RISK_MARK = "<!-- factory-pr-risk -->"
RISK_VERDICT = re.compile(r"^## Risk Assessment: (.+)$", re.MULTILINE)
RISK_HEAD = re.compile(r"Scored head `([0-9a-f]{7,40})`")
PASSED = {"SUCCESS", "NEUTRAL", "SKIPPED"}
# The E2E workflow waits by design until the PR has an approving review or this
# label. It used to fail its status jobs, annotating each with GATE_TITLE; since
# factory-mono#30901 its PLAN_JOB carries GATE_TITLE as a notice and the status
# jobs skip, so their required checks never report (a skipped job's name is its
# unrendered template, matching no required name). The match is the annotation,
# not a check name, so a reworded gate fails loudly again.
GATE_TITLE = "E2E waits for approval"
GATE_LABEL = "e2e:run"
PLAN_JOB = "plan"
# Worst run wins per name, except a cancelled run loses to any other run: a
# concurrency group cancels the duplicate push or pull_request run of a job.
RANK = {"fail": 3, "pending": 2, "gate": 2, "pass": 1, "cancelled": 0}
MERGEABLE = {"CLEAN", "UNSTABLE", "HAS_HOOKS"}
# Review threads come in one page of at most 100; READY never rests on a
# partial view of them. Checks are paginated, since monorepos report hundreds.
THREAD_PAGE = 100
MAX_FAILED_POLLS = 10
TRANSIENT = re.compile(
    r"HTTP 5\d\d|timed? ?out|connection (reset|refused)|EOF|temporar|"
    r"could not resolve host|TLS handshake|Something went wrong",
    re.IGNORECASE,
)
# GitHub words its secondary limit as abuse detection too, with a 403.
RATE_LIMITED = re.compile(r"rate limit|abuse detection|HTTP 429", re.IGNORECASE)
# A 404 or 403 carries no ETag to revalidate against. For classic protection
# it means the token lacks admin, which changes only when the token gains it.
# gh ends its last stderr line with the status; a rate-limit 403 never gets here.
DENIED = re.compile(r"\(HTTP 40[34]\)$")
DENIED_TTL = 24 * 3600


# REST pages hold at most 100 items; the next page's URL comes in the Link header.
PAGE = 100
NEXT = re.compile(r'<([^>]+)>;\s*rel="next"')
# REST exposes no review thread's resolution, so this is the one GraphQL read: a
# few points, made when the PR's review comments changed or the PR is read.
THREADS = """
query($owner: String!, $name: String!, $number: Int!) {
  repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) { pullRequest(number: $number) {
    reviewThreads(first: 100) { nodes { isResolved comments(first: 1) { nodes { databaseId } } } }
  } }
}
"""
# Under this share of GraphQL left, the thread read is skipped.
LOW = 0.20
MIN_INTERVAL = 300
# Pacing assumes this many watchers share the account, and leaves them half of
# what each bucket has left before its reset.
WATCHERS, SHARE = 200, 0.5
# The PR itself is re-read at least every this many polls: its merge state can
# change with nothing on the PR changing, when its base moves.
FULL_EVERY = 6


class GhError(Exception):
    pass


def log(message: str) -> None:
    print(f"pr-watch: {message}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def fail(message: str) -> NoReturn:
    print(f"pr-watch: {message}\nERROR", flush=True)
    sys.exit(2)


def header(head: str, name: str) -> str | None:
    found = re.search(rf"^{name}: *(.+?)\s*$", head, re.IGNORECASE | re.MULTILINE)
    return found and found[1]


class Budget:
    """The rate-limit buckets as the latest responses report them, and the
    calls they counted. GitHub answers one resource from buckets with different
    resets, so each (resource, reset) is a bucket of its own."""

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.buckets: dict[str, Json] = {}
        self.calls = 0

    def record(self, out: str) -> tuple[int, str, str]:
        """A `gh api --include` answer's status, headers, and body. Every
        status but 304 counts against its bucket."""
        head, _, body = out.partition("\r\n\r\n") if "\r\n\r\n" in out else out.partition("\n\n")
        status = re.match(r"HTTP/\S+ (\d+)", head)
        values = [header(head, f"x-ratelimit-{k}") for k in ("resource", "remaining", "limit", "reset")]
        if all(values):
            resource, remaining, limit, reset = values
            self.buckets[f"{resource}@{reset}"] = {
                "resource": resource, "remaining": int(remaining), "limit": int(limit), "reset": int(reset),
            }
        code = int(status[1]) if status else 0
        if code != 304:
            self.calls += 1
        return code, head, body

    def take(self) -> int:
        """The calls counted since the last take."""
        calls, self.calls = self.calls, 0
        return calls

    def low(self, resource: str) -> bool:
        return any(
            b["resource"] == resource and b["remaining"] < LOW * b["limit"] for b in self.buckets.values()
        )

    def pace(self, interval: int, calls: float, now: float) -> int:
        """Seconds until the next poll: at least interval, and long enough that
        calls a poll from WATCHERS watchers, until each bucket resets, spend at
        most SHARE of what it has left. A bucket that one round of every
        watcher would overspend is slept out to its reset."""
        delay = interval
        for key, b in list(self.buckets.items()):
            window = b["reset"] - now
            if window <= 0:
                del self.buckets[key]
                continue
            spend, allowed = calls * WATCHERS, SHARE * b["remaining"]
            if spend > allowed:
                delay = max(delay, math.ceil(window) + 5)
            elif spend:
                delay = max(delay, math.ceil(window * spend / allowed))
        return min(delay, 3605)

    def tightest(self) -> str:
        if not self.buckets:
            return "no budget read yet"
        b = min(self.buckets.values(), key=lambda b: b["remaining"])
        return f"{b['resource']} {b['remaining']}/{b['limit']} until {datetime.fromtimestamp(b['reset'], UTC):%H:%M:%SZ}"


BUDGET = Budget()


def wait_for_rate_limit() -> None:
    """Sleep out a rate limit. A primary limit is spent only when core has 0
    remaining: sleep until its reset. Any other match is GitHub's secondary
    limit, which no bucket reports and which lifts within about a minute, so
    sleeping to a primary reset would blind the watcher for an hour."""
    proc = subprocess.run(["gh", "api", "rate_limit"], check=False, capture_output=True, text=True)
    core = json.loads(proc.stdout)["resources"]["core"] if proc.returncode == 0 else {}
    if core.get("remaining") == 0:
        delay = min(max(core["reset"] - int(time.time()), 0) + 5, 3600)
        log(f"GitHub rate limit spent; sleeping {delay}s until it resets")
    else:
        delay = random.randint(50, 70)
        log(f"GitHub secondary rate limit; sleeping {delay}s")
    time.sleep(delay)


def gh(*args: str, ride: bool = True, unchanged: bool = False) -> str:
    """Run gh, riding out rate limits (unless ride is False: the caller skips
    the read instead) and retrying transient failures with backoff. With
    unchanged, a 304 answers like a success: gh exits 1 on it."""
    delay = 2
    for attempt in range(5):
        proc = subprocess.run(
            ["gh", *args], check=False, capture_output=True, text=True
        )
        if proc.returncode == 0 or (unchanged and "HTTP 304" in proc.stderr):
            return proc.stdout
        message = (
            proc.stderr.strip().splitlines() or [f"gh exited {proc.returncode}"]
        )[-1]
        if RATE_LIMITED.search(proc.stderr) and ride:
            wait_for_rate_limit()
        elif TRANSIENT.search(proc.stderr) and attempt < 4:
            log(f"gh {' '.join(args[:2])}: {message}; retrying in {delay}s")
            time.sleep(delay)
            delay *= 2
        else:
            raise GhError(message)
    raise GhError("gh kept failing")


def graphql(query: str, ride: bool = True, **variables: str | int) -> Json:
    args = ["api", "graphql", "--include", "-f", f"query={query}"]
    for key, value in variables.items():
        args += ["-F" if isinstance(value, int) else "-f", f"{key}={value}"]
    _, _, out = BUDGET.record(gh(*args, ride=ride))
    try:
        data = json.loads(out)["data"]
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError) as error:
        raise GhError(f"GitHub answered no GraphQL data: {snippet(out)}") from error
    if data is None:
        raise GhError(f"GitHub answered no GraphQL data: {snippet(out)}")
    return data


class Rest:
    """GETs by REST as conditional requests. Each URL's ETag and body are kept
    in a file per PR, so restarts reuse them: an unchanged resource answers
    304, which no rate limit counts, and its kept body stands in."""

    def __init__(self, path: Path) -> None:
        self.path = path
        try:
            self.cache: Json = json.loads(path.read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self.cache = {}
        self.read: Json = {}
        self.changed = 0

    def get(self, url: str, fresh: bool = True) -> tuple[Any, str | None]:
        """The body at url and the URL of its next page, if any. Unless fresh,
        a kept body stands in with no request."""
        entry = self.cache.get(url, {})
        if fresh or "body" not in entry:
            tag = ["-H", f"If-None-Match: {entry['etag']}"] if "etag" in entry and "body" in entry else []
            status, head, body = BUDGET.record(gh("api", "--include", *tag, url, unchanged=bool(tag)))
            if status != 304:
                link = header(head, "link")
                entry = {"body": json.loads(body), "next": (m := link and NEXT.search(link)) and m[1]}
                if etag := header(head, "etag"):
                    entry["etag"] = etag
                self.changed += 1
        self.read[url] = entry
        return entry["body"], entry["next"]

    def all(self, url: str, key: str | None = None, fresh: bool = True) -> list[Json]:
        """Every page's items: the list each page is, or its key's list."""
        items: list[Json] = []
        next_url: str | None = url
        while next_url:
            body, next_url = self.get(next_url, fresh)
            items += body[key] if key else body
        return items

    def save(self, extra: Json) -> None:
        """Keep only what this poll read, so a moved head's checks drop out."""
        tmp = self.path.with_suffix(f".{os.getpid()}.tmp")
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(self.read | extra))
        tmp.replace(self.path)
        self.cache, self.read = self.read | extra, {}


def revalidate(source: str, entry: Json, parse: Callable[[Any], list[str]]) -> Json:
    """A source's cache entry, refreshed: {etag, names} from a readable source,
    or {denied} when it 404s or 403s. Only the 200 needs --include, for its
    ETag; gh exits 1 on a 304, which only this conditional request receives."""
    etag = entry.get("etag")
    tag = ["-H", f"If-None-Match: {etag}"] if etag else []
    try:
        status, head, body = BUDGET.record(gh("api", "--include", *tag, source, unchanged=bool(etag)))
    except GhError as error:
        if not DENIED.search(str(error)):
            raise
        return {"denied": time.time()}
    if status == 304:
        return entry
    return {"etag": header(head, "etag"), "names": parse(json.loads(body))}


def snippet(body: str, limit: int = 160) -> str:
    body = re.sub(r"<!--.*?-->|<[^>]+>", " ", body or "", flags=re.DOTALL)
    text = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", html.unescape(body)).strip()
    return text if len(text) <= limit else text[: limit - 3] + "..."


def login(node: Json) -> str:
    return (node["author"] or {}).get("login", "ghost")


def marked(node: Json) -> bool:
    return AGENT_MARK in node["body"]


def posted(node: Json) -> str:
    """When a comment or reply was created, or a review submitted."""
    return node.get("submittedAt") or node["createdAt"]


def human(node: Json) -> bool:
    author = node["author"] or {}
    return author.get("__typename") == "User" and not login(node).startswith(
        SERVICE_PREFIX
    )


def noise(node: Json) -> bool:
    """A bot comment that is no feedback: a status report or Linear's linkback."""
    return not human(node) and (
        any(b in login(node) for b in STATUS_BOTS)
        or (login(node) == LINEAR_BOT and node["body"].startswith(LINKBACK))
    )


def assessment(node: Json, head: str) -> tuple[str, str] | None:
    """The risk assessment's verdict on this head as an event, keyed by head
    and verdict so its in-place rewrites wake once each; None for any other
    comment, a notice that is still waiting or running, or another head's score."""
    body = node["body"]
    if human(node) or not body.startswith(RISK_MARK):
        return None
    verdict, scored = RISK_VERDICT.search(body), RISK_HEAD.search(body)
    if not (verdict and scored and head.startswith(scored[1])):
        return None
    summary = body.split("<details>", 1)[0]
    bullets = [line[2:] for line in summary.splitlines() if line.startswith("- ")][:2]
    return (
        f"risk:{head}:{verdict[1]}",
        f"risk-assessment {verdict[1]} at {head[:12]}: {snippet(' '.join(bullets), 240)} {node['url']}",
    )


def stamp(node: Json) -> str:
    """The version of a note: its latest edit, else its posting."""
    return max(
        filter(None, (posted(node), node["lastEditedAt"])), key=datetime.fromisoformat
    )


def reviews(pr: Json) -> list[Json]:
    return [
        r for r in pr["reviews"]["nodes"] if r["state"] not in ("PENDING", "DISMISSED")
    ]


def replies(thread: Json) -> list[Json]:
    """A thread's comments as everyone else sees them. A pending review
    hides its comments from all but their author, who is the viewer, so a
    reply filed into one answers nothing."""
    return [c for c in thread["comments"]["nodes"] if c["state"] == "SUBMITTED"]


def responded(pr: Json) -> datetime:
    """When the agent last responded: its newest marked comment, review, or
    thread reply, anywhere on the PR."""
    notes = [c for t in pr["reviewThreads"]["nodes"] for c in replies(t)]
    return max(
        (
            datetime.fromisoformat(posted(n))
            for n in pr["comments"]["nodes"] + reviews(pr) + notes
            if marked(n)
        ),
        default=NEVER,
    )


def parse_target(raw: str, repo: str | None) -> tuple[str, int]:
    url = re.fullmatch(
        r"https?://github\.com/([^/\s]+/[^/\s]+)/pull/(\d+)\S*", raw.strip()
    )
    number = re.fullmatch(r"#?(\d+)", raw.strip())
    if not (url or number):
        fail(f"'{raw}' is not a PR number or URL")
    pr = int((url or number).group(2 if url else 1))
    repo = repo or (url.group(1) if url else None)
    if not repo:
        remote = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "remote", "get-url", "origin"], check=False, capture_output=True, text=True
        ).stdout.strip()
        found = re.search(r"github\.com[:/]([^/\s]+/[^/\s]+?)(?:\.git)?$", remote)
        if not found:
            fail("no --repo given and the current directory has no GitHub origin remote")
        repo = found[1]
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[^/\s]+/[^/\s]+", repo):
        fail(f"'{repo}' is not an owner/name repo")
    return repo, pr


def bucket(node: Json, gates: set[str]) -> str:
    if node["__typename"] == "CheckRun":
        if node["id"] in gates:
            return "gate"
        if node["status"] != "COMPLETED":
            return "pending"
        if node["conclusion"] == "CANCELLED":
            return "cancelled"
        return "pass" if node["conclusion"] in PASSED else "fail"
    return {"SUCCESS": "pass", "FAILURE": "fail", "ERROR": "fail"}.get(
        node["state"], "pending"
    )


def contexts(pr: Json) -> Json:
    commits = pr["commits"]["nodes"]
    rollup = commits[0]["commit"]["statusCheckRollup"] if commits else None
    return (rollup or {}).get("contexts") or {"nodes": []}


def collapse_checks(pr: Json, gates: set[str]) -> dict[str, Json]:
    """One entry per check name with its pass, pending, gate, or fail bucket; a
    job's push and pull_request runs share a name, and either failing fails the
    job."""
    checks: dict[str, Json] = {}
    for node in contexts(pr)["nodes"]:
        name = node.get("name") or node.get("context")
        entry = {
            "bucket": bucket(node, gates),
            "url": node.get("detailsUrl") or node.get("targetUrl") or "",
        }
        if name not in checks or RANK[entry["bucket"]] > RANK[checks[name]["bucket"]]:
            checks[name] = entry
    for entry in checks.values():
        if entry["bucket"] == "cancelled":
            entry["bucket"] = "fail"
    return checks


class Watcher:
    def __init__(self, repo: str, number: int, interval: int, once: bool) -> None:
        self.repo, self.number, self.interval, self.once = repo, number, interval, once
        self.owner, self.name = repo.split("/")
        slug = f"{repo.replace('/', '__')}__{number}"
        self.state_path = STATE_DIR / f"{slug}.json"
        self.lock_path = STATE_DIR / f"{slug}.lock"
        self.reported: set[str] = set()
        if not once and self.state_path.exists():
            self.reported = set(json.loads(self.state_path.read_text()))
        self.events: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
        self.required: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
        self.previous: Any = None
        self.status = ""
        self.costs: list[int] = []
        self.polls = 0
        self.fresh = True
        self.delay = interval
        self.rest = Rest(STATE_DIR / f"{slug}.rest.json")
        self.threads: Json = {}
        self.started = SELF.stat().st_mtime

    def lock(self) -> Any:
        STATE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        # Held open for the life of the process; the OS drops the lock on exit.
        handle = open(self.lock_path, "a+")  # noqa: SIM115
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            handle.seek(0)
            pid = handle.read().strip() or "unknown"
            fail(
                f"pid {pid} already watches {self.repo}#{self.number}; kill it only if its exit never reaches you"
            )
        handle.seek(0)
        handle.truncate()
        handle.write(str(os.getpid()))
        handle.flush()
        return handle

    def save(self) -> None:
        tmp = self.state_path.with_suffix(".tmp")
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(sorted(self.reported)))
        tmp.replace(self.state_path)

    def finish(self, verdict: str, detail: str, code: int) -> NoReturn:
        self.rest.save({"threads": self.threads})
        for key, line in self.events:
            print(line, flush=True)
            self.reported.add(key)
        print(f"{verdict} {self.repo}#{self.number} {detail}".rstrip(), flush=True)
        # A lock file outlives only a watcher that died without a verdict, which
        # is what --check looks for.
        if not self.once:
            self.lock_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        if verdict in ("MERGED", "CLOSED"):
            self.state_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        elif self.events and not self.once:
            self.save()
        sys.exit(code)

    def emit(self, key: str, line: str) -> None:
        """Queue an event unless an earlier run reported it. Keys become
        reported only when printed, so a poll that fails midway loses nothing."""
        if key not in self.reported:
            self.events.append((key, line))

    def note(self, node: Json, **fields: Any) -> Json:
        """A REST comment or review in the shape the evaluation reads. REST
        names bots `<app>[bot]`; the bare login matches STATUS_BOTS and LINEAR_BOT."""
        user = node.get("user") or {}
        updated = node.get("updated_at")
        return {
            "id": node["node_id"],
            "url": node["html_url"],
            "body": node.get("body") or "",
            "createdAt": node.get("created_at") or node.get("submitted_at"),
            "lastEditedAt": updated if updated and updated != node.get("created_at") else None,
            "author": user
            and {
                "login": user["login"].removesuffix("[bot]"),
                "__typename": "Bot" if user["type"] == "Bot" else "User",
            },
            **fields,
        }

    def fetch(self) -> Json:
        """The PR, its head's checks, and its feedback: the head by git, the
        rest by REST, and the PR itself only when the module docstring says."""
        repo, n = f"repos/{self.repo}", self.number
        url = f"{repo}/pulls/{n}"
        kept = self.rest.cache.get(url, {}).get("body")
        head = None if self.once or kept is None else self.remote_head(kept)
        self.fresh = head is None
        if self.fresh:
            p, _ = self.rest.get(url)
            head = p["head"]["sha"]
        before = self.rest.changed
        runs = self.rest.all(f"{repo}/commits/{head}/check-runs?per_page={PAGE}", "check_runs")
        statuses = self.rest.all(f"{repo}/commits/{head}/status?per_page={PAGE}", "statuses")
        settled = self.rest.changed > before and all(r["status"] == "completed" for r in runs)
        before = self.rest.changed
        comments = self.rest.all(f"{repo}/issues/{n}/comments?per_page={PAGE}")
        reviewed = self.rest.all(f"{repo}/pulls/{n}/reviews?per_page={PAGE}")
        notes = self.rest.all(f"{repo}/pulls/{n}/comments?per_page={PAGE}")
        if not self.fresh:
            self.fresh = (
                head != kept["head"]["sha"] or settled or self.rest.changed > before or self.polls % FULL_EVERY == 0
            )
            p, _ = self.rest.get(url, self.fresh)
        self.polls += 1
        pending = {r["id"] for r in reviewed if r["state"] == "PENDING"}
        latest: dict[str, str] = {}
        for r in reviewed:
            if r["state"] in ("APPROVED", "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "DISMISSED") and r["user"]:
                latest[r["user"]["login"]] = r["state"]
        threads: dict[int, list[Json]] = {}
        for c in sorted(notes, key=lambda c: c["created_at"]):
            threads.setdefault(c.get("in_reply_to_id") or c["id"], []).append(c)
        resolved = self.resolution(notes)
        return {
            "url": p["html_url"],
            "state": "MERGED" if p["merged_at"] else p["state"].upper(),
            "isDraft": p["draft"],
            "headRefOid": head,
            "baseRefName": p["base"]["ref"],
            "baseRef": {"target": {"oid": p["base"]["sha"]}},
            "mergeStateStatus": (p.get("mergeable_state") or "unknown").upper(),
            "reviewDecision": None,
            "labels": {"nodes": p["labels"]},
            "latestOpinionatedReviews": {"nodes": [{"state": s} for s in latest.values() if s != "DISMISSED"]},
            "commits": {"nodes": [{"commit": {"statusCheckRollup": {"contexts": {"nodes": [
                *({"__typename": "CheckRun", "id": r["id"], "name": r["name"], "status": r["status"].upper(),
                   "conclusion": (r["conclusion"] or "").upper() or None, "detailsUrl": r["html_url"] or r["details_url"]}
                  for r in runs),
                *({"__typename": "StatusContext", "context": s["context"], "state": s["state"].upper(),
                   "targetUrl": s["target_url"]} for s in statuses),
            ]}}}}]},
            "comments": {"nodes": [self.note(c) for c in comments]},
            # A review's body can be edited with no REST timestamp, so its id
            # carries the body's digest: an edit is a new version.
            "reviews": {"nodes": [
                self.note(r, id=f"{r['node_id']}:{hashlib.sha1((r.get('body') or '').encode()).hexdigest()[:8]}",
                          state=r["state"], submittedAt=r.get("submitted_at"),
                          comments={"totalCount": sum(c.get("pull_request_review_id") == r["id"] for c in notes)})
                for r in reviewed
            ]},
            "reviewThreads": {"totalCount": len(threads), "nodes": [
                {
                    "isResolved": resolved.get(str(root), False),
                    "path": t[0]["path"],
                    "line": t[0].get("line") or t[0].get("original_line"),
                    "comments": {"nodes": [
                        self.note(c, state="PENDING" if c.get("pull_request_review_id") in pending else "SUBMITTED")
                        for c in t
                    ]},
                }
                for root, t in threads.items()
            ]},
        }

    def remote_head(self, pr: Json) -> str | None:
        """The PR's head by `git ls-remote`, which spends no API budget; None
        once its head branch in this repository is gone (merged, or closed and
        deleted), so that the PR itself is read."""
        refs = [f"refs/pull/{self.number}/head"]
        own = (pr["head"]["repo"] or {}).get("full_name") == self.repo
        if own:
            refs.append(f"refs/heads/{pr['head']['ref']}")
        try:
            proc = subprocess.run(
                ["git", "-c", "credential.helper=", "-c", "credential.helper=!gh auth git-credential",
                 "ls-remote", f"https://github.com/{self.repo}.git", *refs],
                check=False, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120,
            )
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as error:
            raise GhError("git ls-remote timed out") from error
        if proc.returncode:
            raise GhError(f"git ls-remote: {(proc.stderr.strip().splitlines() or ['failed'])[-1]}")
        found = {ref: sha for sha, ref in (line.split("\t") for line in proc.stdout.splitlines())}
        if own and refs[1] not in found:
            return None
        return found.get(refs[0])

    def resolution(self, notes: list[Json]) -> dict[str, bool]:
        """Each thread's resolution by its first comment's id, read by GraphQL
        when the review comments changed or the PR itself was read this poll,
        and the GraphQL budget is not low: resolving or reopening a thread
        edits no comment. Unread threads count as unresolved."""
        version = hashlib.sha1(json.dumps(sorted((c["id"], c["updated_at"]) for c in notes)).encode()).hexdigest()
        kept = self.rest.cache.get("threads") or {}
        if not notes or (kept.get("version") == version and not self.fresh) or BUDGET.low("graphql"):
            self.threads = kept
            return kept.get("resolved", {})
        try:
            data = graphql(THREADS, ride=False, owner=self.owner, name=self.name, number=self.number)
        except GhError as error:
            log(f"thread resolution unread: {error}")
            self.threads = kept
            return kept.get("resolved", {})
        nodes = data["repository"]["pullRequest"]["reviewThreads"]["nodes"]
        resolved = {str(t["comments"]["nodes"][0]["databaseId"]): t["isResolved"] for t in nodes if t["comments"]["nodes"]}
        self.threads = {"version": version, "resolved": resolved}
        return resolved

    def landing(self, pr: Json) -> str:
        """The branch the PR finally lands in, as the module docstring defines it."""
        branch, seen = pr["baseRefName"], {pr["baseRefName"]}
        while True:
            heads = self.rest.all(
                f"repos/{self.repo}/pulls?state=open&per_page={PAGE}&head={quote(f'{self.owner}:{branch}', safe=':')}",
                fresh=self.fresh,
            )
            above = [
                h["base"]["ref"]
                for h in heads
                if h["head"]["ref"] == branch
                and h["base"]["repo"]["full_name"] == self.repo
                and (h["head"]["repo"] or {}).get("full_name") == self.repo
            ]
            if not above:
                return branch
            if above[0] in seen:
                raise GhError(
                    f"the stack under {pr['baseRefName']} loops back to {above[0]}"
                )
            branch = above[0]
            seen.add(branch)

    def gating(self, pr: Json, checks: dict[str, Json]) -> set[str]:
        """The checks that gate, as the module docstring defines them."""
        landing = self.landing(pr)
        required = self.required_checks(landing)
        if not required:
            return set(checks)
        return required if landing == pr["baseRefName"] else required & set(checks)

    def gates(self, pr: Json) -> tuple[set[str], bool]:
        """Whether the E2E approval gate is waiting (GATE_TITLE on a failed or
        plan run of the head), and its failed runs. Asked only while the PR has
        neither an approval nor the label, each run's conditionally on every poll:
        a run can be rerequested or updated and gain annotations."""
        if any(
            r["state"] == "APPROVED" for r in pr["latestOpinionatedReviews"]["nodes"]
        ) or any(label["name"] == GATE_LABEL for label in pr["labels"]["nodes"]):
            return set(), False
        runs = {
            n["id"]: n["conclusion"] == "FAILURE"
            for n in contexts(pr)["nodes"]
            if n["__typename"] == "CheckRun"
            and (n["conclusion"] == "FAILURE" or n["name"] == PLAN_JOB)
        }
        if not runs:
            return set(), False
        annotated = {
            run
            for run in runs
            if any(
                a["title"] == GATE_TITLE
                for a in self.rest.all(f"repos/{self.repo}/check-runs/{run}/annotations?per_page={PAGE}")
            )
        }
        return {run for run in annotated if runs[run]}, bool(annotated)

    def required_checks(self, base: str) -> set[str]:
        """Required check names per base, so a required check that has not
        started counts as pending instead of passing by omission. Rulesets are
        readable with read access; classic protection needs admin and 404s or
        403s otherwise. Any other failure propagates so the next poll retries.
        Every process shares one cache per base and revalidates it by ETag: a
        304 costs no rate limit."""
        if base not in self.required:
            path = (
                STATE_DIR / "required" / f"{quote(f'{self.repo}:{base}', safe='')}.json"
            )
            try:
                cache: Json = json.loads(path.read_text())
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                cache = {}
            sources = {
                f"repos/{self.repo}/rules/branches/{base}": lambda rules: [
                    check["context"]
                    for rule in rules
                    if rule["type"] == "required_status_checks"
                    for check in rule["parameters"]["required_status_checks"]
                ],
                f"repos/{self.repo}/branches/{base}/protection/required_status_checks": lambda protection: [
                    *protection.get("contexts", []),
                    *(check["context"] for check in protection.get("checks", [])),
                ],
            }
            names: set[str] = set()
            for source, parse in sources.items():
                entry = cache.get(source, {})
                if time.time() - entry.get("denied", 0) >= DENIED_TTL:
                    entry = cache[source] = revalidate(source, entry, parse)
                names.update(entry.get("names", []))
            path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            tmp = path.with_suffix(f".{os.getpid()}.tmp")
            tmp.write_text(json.dumps(cache))
            tmp.replace(path)
            self.required[base] = names
            log(
                f"required checks on {base}: "
                + (", ".join(sorted(names)) or "none required, so every check gates")
            )
        return self.required[base]

    def feedback(self, pr: Json) -> None:
        """Queue every feedback item open now, as the module docstring defines it."""
        latest = responded(pr)

        def fresh(node: Json) -> bool:
            return not marked(node) and datetime.fromisoformat(stamp(node)) > latest

        for c in pr["comments"]["nodes"]:
            if fresh(c) and not noise(c):
                self.emit(
                    f"c:{c['id']}:{stamp(c)}",
                    f"comment from {login(c)}: {snippet(c['body'])} {c['url']}",
                )
        for r in reviews(pr):
            if fresh(r) and (r["state"] == "CHANGES_REQUESTED" or r["body"].strip()):
                state = r["state"].lower().replace("_", " ")
                text = f": {snippet(r['body'])}" if r["body"].strip() else ""
                self.emit(
                    f"c:{r['id']}:{stamp(r)}",
                    f"review from {login(r)} ({state}){text} {r['url']}",
                )
        for t in pr["reviewThreads"]["nodes"]:
            nodes = replies(t)
            if t["isResolved"] or not nodes or marked(nodes[-1]):
                continue
            last = nodes[-1]
            where = f"{t['path']}:{t['line']}" if t["line"] else t["path"]
            self.emit(
                f"c:{last['id']}:{stamp(last)}",
                f"thread from {login(last)} on {where}: {snippet(last['body'])} {last['url']}",
            )

    def evaluate(
        self,
        pr: Json,
        checks: dict[str, Json],
        gating: set[str],
        stable: bool,
    ) -> tuple[list[tuple[str, str]], list[str]]:
        """Why the head cannot merge now: (key, line) actions the agent must
        handle, and wait lines for states that resolve without it."""
        head, base, state = pr["headRefOid"], pr["baseRefName"], pr["mergeStateStatus"]
        base_oid = ((pr["baseRef"] or {}).get("target") or {}).get("oid", "")
        actions: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
        waits: list[str] = []

        if pr["reviewThreads"]["totalCount"] > THREAD_PAGE:
            actions.append(
                (
                    f"incomplete:{head}",
                    f"incomplete: more than {THREAD_PAGE} review threads, so check them by hand before merging",
                )
            )
        # Only the viewer's own pending review is visible, and GitHub allows
        # one per account per PR.
        for r in pr["reviews"]["nodes"]:
            if r["state"] == "PENDING":
                count = r["comments"]["totalCount"]
                actions.append(
                    (
                        f"pending-review:{r['id']}:{count}",
                        f"pending-review: your unsubmitted review hides comments ({count}) from everyone else {r['url']}",
                    )
                )
        if state == "DIRTY":
            actions.append(
                (
                    f"conflict:{head}:{base_oid}",
                    f"conflict: the branch conflicts with {base}",
                )
            )
        if state == "BEHIND":
            actions.append(
                (
                    f"behind:{head}:{base_oid}",
                    f"behind: branch protection requires the branch to be current with {base}",
                )
            )
        for name in sorted(gating):
            entry = checks.get(name, {"bucket": "pending", "url": ""})
            if entry["bucket"] == "fail":
                actions.append(
                    (
                        f"fail:{head}:{name}:{entry['url']}",
                        f"check-failed {name} (gating) {entry['url']}",
                    )
                )
        pending = sorted(
            n
            for n in gating | set(checks)
            if checks.get(n, {"bucket": "pending"})["bucket"] == "pending"
        )
        gated = sorted(n for n, c in checks.items() if c["bucket"] == "gate")
        if pending:
            waits.append(f"pending checks ({len(pending)}): {', '.join(pending[:5])}")
        elif not stable:
            waits.append("checks settling")
        if gated:
            waits.append(
                f"E2E gate ({len(gated)} checks): runs once approved or labelled {GATE_LABEL}"
            )
        if pr["isDraft"]:
            waits.append("draft")
        decision = pr["reviewDecision"]
        opinions = {r["state"] for r in pr["latestOpinionatedReviews"]["nodes"]}
        approved = decision == "APPROVED" or (
            decision is None
            and "APPROVED" in opinions
            and "CHANGES_REQUESTED" not in opinions
        )
        if not approved:
            waits.append(
                f"review: {(decision or 'no approval').lower().replace('_', ' ')}"
            )
        if actions or waits:
            return actions, waits

        unresolved = [
            notes[0]["url"]
            for t in pr["reviewThreads"]["nodes"]
            if not t["isResolved"] and (notes := replies(t))
        ]
        if unresolved:
            return [
                (
                    f"unresolved:{head}:{base_oid}:{len(unresolved)}",
                    f"unresolved review threads ({len(unresolved)}): {' '.join(unresolved)}",
                )
            ], []
        # REST has no review decision: an approval that leaves the PR BLOCKED is
        # one branch protection does not count yet (a code owner's is missing).
        if state == "BLOCKED":
            return [], ["blocked: GitHub reports BLOCKED, so a required review (code owner or count), ruleset or merge queue is unmet"]
        if state not in MERGEABLE:
            return [], [f"merge state {state}"]
        return [], []

    def poll(self) -> None:
        self.events = []
        pr = self.fetch()
        head = pr["headRefOid"]
        if pr["state"] == "MERGED":
            self.finish("MERGED", pr["url"], 0)
        if pr["state"] == "CLOSED":
            self.finish("CLOSED", pr["url"], 1)
        failed, waiting = self.gates(pr)
        checks = collapse_checks(pr, failed)
        gating = self.gating(pr, checks)
        if waiting:
            checks |= {n: {"bucket": "gate", "url": ""} for n in gating - set(checks)}
        # What only the agent can judge: a watcher wakes once on each, and
        # --once lists them without letting them set its verdict.
        advisory = [
            (f"fail:{head}:{name}:{entry['url']}", f"check-failed {name} (optional) {entry['url']}")
            for name, entry in sorted(checks.items())
            if entry["bucket"] == "fail" and name not in gating
        ]
        advisory += filter(None, (assessment(c, head) for c in pr["comments"]["nodes"]))
        if self.once:
            self.feedback(pr)
            actions, waits = self.evaluate(pr, checks, gating, stable=True)
            self.events += actions
            verdict, code = (
                ("ACTION", 1) if self.events else ("WAIT", 3) if waits else ("READY", 0)
            )
            self.events += advisory + [("", f"waiting: {w}") for w in waits]
            self.finish(verdict, f"@ {head}", code)

        # Checks register a few seconds after a push; two identical polls in a
        # row keep a half-registered (or still empty) set from reading as green.
        snapshot = (
            head,
            sorted((n, c["bucket"]) for n, c in checks.items()),
            pr["mergeStateStatus"],
        )
        stable, self.previous = snapshot == self.previous, snapshot

        self.feedback(pr)
        for key, line in advisory:
            self.emit(key, line)
        actions, waits = self.evaluate(pr, checks, gating, stable)
        for key, line in actions:
            self.emit(key, line)
        if self.events:
            self.finish("ACTION", f"@ {head}", 1)
        if not actions and not waits:
            self.finish("READY", f"@ {head}", 0)
        status = f"{self.repo}#{self.number} @ {head[:7]}: " + "; ".join(
            waits or ["holding: every action here was already reported"]
        )
        if status != self.status:
            self.status = status
            log(status)

    def run(self) -> NoReturn:
        failures = 0
        while True:
            try:
                self.poll()
                self.rest.save({"threads": self.threads})
                failures = 0
            except (GhError, KeyError, TypeError, ValueError) as error:
                failures += 1
                log(f"poll failed ({failures}/{MAX_FAILED_POLLS}): {error}")
                if self.once or failures >= MAX_FAILED_POLLS:
                    self.events = []
                    self.finish("ERROR", f"GitHub failed: {error}", 2)
            self.sleep()

    def sleep(self) -> None:
        self.costs = [*self.costs, BUDGET.take()][-FULL_EVERY:]
        calls = sum(self.costs) / len(self.costs)
        delay = BUDGET.pace(self.interval, calls, time.time())
        if delay != self.delay:
            self.delay = delay
            log(
                f"{calls:.2f} counted calls a poll (last {len(self.costs)}: {self.costs}); "
                f"tightest budget {BUDGET.tightest()}; polling every {delay}s"
            )
        time.sleep(delay)
        # agents-pull fast-forwards ~/.agents every 15 minutes: run what it
        # brought. The lock fd closes on exec, and the new process takes it.
        if SELF.stat().st_mtime != self.started:
            log("pr-watch changed on disk; restarting into it")
            os.execv(sys.executable, [sys.executable, str(SELF), *sys.argv[1:]])


def check() -> NoReturn:
    """List each watcher on this machine: alive, or dead without a verdict (a
    droid daemon restart kills its background jobs with no exit notice), with
    the command that restarts it. Exit 1 when any is dead."""
    dead = 0
    for path in sorted(STATE_DIR.glob("*.lock")):
        owner, name, number = path.stem.rsplit("__", 2)
        url = f"https://github.com/{owner}/{name}/pull/{number}"
        with open(path, "a+") as handle:
            try:
                fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            except BlockingIOError:
                handle.seek(0)
                print(f"alive {url} pid {handle.read().strip()}")
                continue
        dead += 1
        print(f"dead {url}: restart with {SELF} {url}")
    sys.exit(1 if dead else 0)


def main() -> None:
    if sys.argv[1:] == ["--check"]:
        check()
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="pr-watch", description="Block until a GitHub PR needs the agent."
    )
    parser.add_argument("pr", help="PR number or URL (or --check alone: list this machine's watchers, alive or dead)")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--repo", help="owner/name (default: from the URL or the current checkout)"
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--interval",
        type=int,
        default=MIN_INTERVAL,
        help=f"fastest seconds between polls; a low budget slows them (default and minimum {MIN_INTERVAL})",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--once", action="store_true", help="evaluate the merge gate once and exit"
    )
    args = parser.parse_args()
    repo, number = parse_target(args.pr, args.repo)
    watcher = Watcher(repo, number, max(args.interval, MIN_INTERVAL), args.once)
    _lock = None if args.once else watcher.lock()
    watcher.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        main()
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        sys.exit(130)
